        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T01:53:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The API require the permissions unconditionaly of which profile is being used:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Bluetooth/framework/java/android/bluetooth/BluetoothAdapter.java;l\u003d2147;drc\u003dcd5ef3ec7ebca06cc03fad23279bb8eee50043ed\n\nAny caller of the API should already have the permission. If they don\u0027t they are abusing a flaw of the stack.\n\nCurrently this permission is enforce far in the headsetService, when reaching phoneStateChanged or clccresponse.\n\nI believe this change is necessary and keep the code healthy.\nIf we want to keep previous behavior, we should add a conditional on the permission and document what is conditional and what is not.",
      "parentUuid": "60245917_bf559e64",
      "revId": "2088fcdabf79621a535f050a38384861c426e27d",
